"""Dogecoin block explorer for Umbrel, on your own Dogecoin Core node (Python standard library only).

Reads everything from the Dogecoin Core app's RPC: blocks (parsed from the raw block, AuxPoW included),
transactions and the mempool. Serves:

  /                      latest blocks and the mempool
  /block/<hash|height>   a block with its transactions, each drawn from sender address to receiver address
  /verified              the verified donation addresses of organisations that help animals (also /address/<address>, /api/v1/verified-addresses)
  /tx/<txid>             a transaction (mempool, a block from this explorer, or any tx with -txindex)
  /search?q=             height, block hash or txid
  /api/v1/blocks         the last blocks, in mempool's format (for hashes.space)
  /api/v1/fees/mempool-blocks   the mempool cut into blocks of 1 MB, best fee first
  /api/blocks/tip/height
  /fee-sorting, /coinbase-merkle, /block-assembly, /block-candidate   the four blocks of the Find Mempool page, one page each (and as .json): the block your node would build
  /api/v1/mining/hashrate/<period>  global hashrate and difficulty, from your node (period: 24h, 14d, 1m, 6m, 1y)
  /api/v1/mining/pools/<period>     blocks per mining pool over the period (a sample of the blocks for the long ones)
  /api/v1/mining/pool-hashrate/<period>  the hashrate of the mining pools together: the network's hashrate times the share of blocks that pools mined
  /api/v1/mining/solo/<period>      the hashrate of the miners that use no pool: blocks whose coinbase names no known pool, times the network's hashrate (an upper bound)
  (1y and 1w are what older versions of the page ask for, and are still answered)
  /api/v1/ws             mempool's WebSocket: {"action":"want","data":["blocks","mempool-blocks"]}

Fees are in koinu per byte (1 DOGE = 100,000,000 koinu).
"""

